title: Payers › Workflow Builder › Configure a step › Documents
route: /payers/summit?tab=builder
intro: Document steps ask for items from the payer's own document list for the workflow's services. The list is edited in Rules & Instructions, never copied into the workflow. A step that names no items asks for every item on the list.
dir: TD
---
start s1 "Select Collect documents, Validate documents or Missing information"
screen cl "'Required documents'\n'Summit Medicaid HMO's document list for Residential 3.5 has 9 items. 9 chosen.'\nOne checkbox per item with its requirement and level of care"
decision d1 "Does the payer have a list for these services?"
screen e1 "'This payer has no document list for these services yet.'"
click c1 "Tick or untick items"
process p1 "The count follows: '2 chosen'\nWith none chosen the step asks for every item on the list"
click c2 "Click 'Choose all' or 'Clear'"
process p2 "All items chosen, or none (so every item is asked for)"
decision d2 "Is a chosen item no longer on the payer's list?"
screen w1 "'N chosen items are no longer on the payer's list. Choose again, or clear them.'"
click c3 "Click 'Edit the list in Rules & Instructions'"
decision d3 "Unsaved changes?"
overlay o1 "'Leave without saving?'"
process p3 "Opens Rules & Instructions on the Clinical documentation group"
process p4 "Edits are held in the builder until 'Save draft'"
end e2 "The step names the documents it needs"
goto g1 "Continues in: Payers › Rules & Instructions › Read the document list"
goto g2 "Continues in: Payers › Test Workflow › Run a test case"

s1 --> cl --> d1
d1 -->|No| e1
d1 -->|Yes| c1 --> p1 --> d2
cl --> c2 --> p2 --> d2
d2 -->|Yes| w1 --> p4
d2 -->|No| p4
cl --> c3 --> d3
d3 -->|Yes| o1 --> p3
d3 -->|No| p3
p3 --> g1
p4 --> e2 --> g2
